WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.870
- What's up?

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:03.330
We're back with the cast
of Abbott Elementary!

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.153
Quinta Brunson, Sheryl Lee
Ralph and Lisa Ann Walter.

00:00:06.013 --> 00:00:07.590
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:10.200
It's amazing how much of school we forget

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.882
by the time we're, you
know, older. (chuckling)

00:00:12.882 --> 00:00:13.950
(audience laughing)

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.420
Makes you wonder how we'd do

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.790
on an elementary school pop quiz,

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.680
if we had to take one
right now, which you do,

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:20.811
'cause I'm making all of us.

00:00:20.811 --> 00:00:21.644
(guests laughing)

00:00:21.644 --> 00:00:22.477
Because it's time to play:

00:00:22.477 --> 00:00:25.500
"Just how fast can you pass this class?"

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.779
- [Sheryl] Oh God.

00:00:26.779 --> 00:00:28.075
(gentle music)

00:00:28.075 --> 00:00:30.212
♪ Just how fast can you pass this class ♪

00:00:30.212 --> 00:00:32.205
- Woo!
- Oh my God! (laughing)

00:00:32.205 --> 00:00:33.660
(audience laughing)

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.300
I had not heard that, I'm very into it.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.133
All right.

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.880
Teams are me and Sheryl.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.536
We are not confident.

00:00:40.536 --> 00:00:42.060
- We're not confident.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.620
- Versus Quinta and Lisa.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.013
- Woo!
- I am extremely confident.

00:00:45.013 --> 00:00:46.648
- We're very confident, very competitive.

00:00:46.648 --> 00:00:48.690
- We're just keeping it real over here,

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:49.523
okay.
- Thank you.

00:00:49.523 --> 00:00:51.180
- Here to host, please welcome

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.310
one of Quinta's fellow Philadelphia girls

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:54.600
and star of "The Office,"

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.010
you can see her and Jane Lynch

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.470
on their "A Swingin' Little
Christmas" tour this December.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:01.071
Here's Kate Flannery, everybody.

00:01:01.071 --> 00:01:03.748
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:01:03.748 --> 00:01:06.831
(upbeat jazzy music)

00:01:11.321 --> 00:01:13.433
- No favoritism, no
favoritism, no favoritism.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:17.610
- No favoritism, I love it. (laughing)

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.960
Well, thank you for hosting.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:19.793
- Thank you!

00:01:19.793 --> 00:01:21.810
- Okay, will you please explain the game?

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:23.610
- This is how, this is
actually what's gonna happen.

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.460
It's a super fast test to
measure how much you remember

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:27.630
from elementary school.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:28.696
- Nothing.

00:01:28.696 --> 00:01:30.000
(everyone laughing)

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.833
- Oh, no.

00:01:30.833 --> 00:01:33.450
I will read two real quiz
questions from each grade.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.970
Each grade's questions are
worth that many points.

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:37.830
For instance, third grade is three points.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:38.663
You get it, right?

00:01:38.663 --> 00:01:39.600
- [Quinta] Okay, okay.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.808
- Is there money involved?

00:01:40.808 --> 00:01:41.641
(audience laughing)

00:01:41.641 --> 00:01:42.474
- [Sheryl] No.

00:01:42.474 --> 00:01:43.307
- Some incentive? No?

00:01:43.307 --> 00:01:45.900
- Okay, if Quinta and Lisa win,

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.047
they get their photo up on

00:01:47.047 --> 00:01:50.327
"The Chicks Wall of Champs
who beat Kelly Clarkson."

00:01:50.327 --> 00:01:51.607
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:01:51.607 --> 00:01:53.677
(triumphant music)

00:01:53.677 --> 00:01:55.170
- Dumb wall, it's a dumb wall.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.417
- She's very competitive.

00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:58.050
- What? Never.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.400
- Me too, but I always lose so-

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.740
- Yeah, but I don't mind,

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:01.709
but you gotta just be competitive.

00:02:01.709 --> 00:02:03.586
- I watch the Emmys, I think
you won, I'm just saying.

00:02:03.586 --> 00:02:06.086
- Part of this career is
losing on game shows on TV,

00:02:06.086 --> 00:02:07.577
(all laughing)

00:02:07.577 --> 00:02:08.410
and I'm tired of it.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:09.243
- All right, class.

00:02:09.243 --> 00:02:10.320
I need your attention.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.153
- Okay.
- Here we go.

00:02:11.153 --> 00:02:12.240
- Yes, teacher.
- Starting-

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.860
Okay, starting with third grade.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:14.910
Three points per question.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.050
Here we go.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:17.790
Ducks fly south for the winter.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.066
This is an example of what behavior?

00:02:20.066 --> 00:02:21.150
(buzzer ringing)

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:21.983
- Migration.

00:02:21.983 --> 00:02:22.993
(bell dinging)

00:02:22.993 --> 00:02:24.311
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:02:24.311 --> 00:02:25.160
- I didn't hit it fast enough.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:26.903
(all women talking indistinctly)

00:02:26.903 --> 00:02:28.311
(audience clapping)

00:02:28.311 --> 00:02:30.060
- And here's the second
third-grade question.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:30.893
Okay.

00:02:30.893 --> 00:02:33.570
What is the area of a rectangle

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:37.444
with the base of four inches
and a width of five inches?

00:02:37.444 --> 00:02:38.609
(buzzer ringing)

00:02:38.609 --> 00:02:39.442
(timer ticking)

00:02:39.442 --> 00:02:40.275
Lisa.

00:02:40.275 --> 00:02:41.108
- 20 inches.

00:02:41.108 --> 00:02:42.774
(bell dinging)
- Yeah, right?

00:02:42.774 --> 00:02:44.401
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:02:44.401 --> 00:02:45.234
I was too nervous.

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:47.130
I was like, "Don't look dumb."

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:49.104
So I didn't press it and
I was, thought 20, damn.

00:02:49.104 --> 00:02:49.954
- You should do

00:02:49.954 --> 00:02:51.120
more game shows, Lisa.
- It was five times four.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:51.953
- She does.

00:02:51.953 --> 00:02:53.482
It's the reason I became a writer.

00:02:53.482 --> 00:02:55.650
(all laughing)

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.750
- All right, here we go, fourth grade.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:59.141
Okay, here we go, fourth grade.

00:02:59.141 --> 00:02:59.974
- Oh God.

00:02:59.974 --> 00:03:01.560
- Okay, the first 10 amendments

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.132
to the Constitution are
also known as the what?

00:03:04.132 --> 00:03:04.965
(buzzer ringing)

00:03:04.965 --> 00:03:05.798
- The Bill of Rights?

00:03:05.798 --> 00:03:06.631
(bell dinging)

00:03:06.631 --> 00:03:07.641
- You are correct.

00:03:07.641 --> 00:03:08.474
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:03:08.474 --> 00:03:09.307
- I'm gonna start getting more bold.

00:03:09.307 --> 00:03:10.992
I'm gonna start getting more bold.

00:03:10.992 --> 00:03:11.825
'Cause I think I'm right

00:03:11.825 --> 00:03:13.200
and then I think I'm gonna look stupid.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.160
- I just like standing

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.594
next to the winner.
- You have two sports Emmys.

00:03:15.594 --> 00:03:17.246
- [Kate] Yes, exactly.

00:03:17.246 --> 00:03:19.710
(all laughing and clapping)

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:21.300
- Stupid? How dare you?

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.214
- Just another reason to
drink, ladies and gentlemen.

00:03:23.214 --> 00:03:24.047
(audience laughing)
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:24.047 --> 00:03:25.200
- Okay, one more fourth grade question.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.033
Here we go.

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:26.866
- [Sheryl] Fourth grade.

00:03:26.866 --> 00:03:28.595
- How do you spell manatee?

00:03:28.595 --> 00:03:29.428
(buzzer ringing)

00:03:29.428 --> 00:03:30.287
- I got it.

00:03:30.287 --> 00:03:32.850
M-A-N-A-T-E-E.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:33.911
- That's it.
(musical trill)

00:03:33.911 --> 00:03:34.744
(bell dinging)
- She's right.

00:03:34.744 --> 00:03:35.577
- You are correct.

00:03:35.577 --> 00:03:36.556
Quinta is correct.

00:03:36.556 --> 00:03:37.454
- We got that.
- I didn't know that.

00:03:37.454 --> 00:03:38.287
- I was about to be like,

00:03:38.287 --> 00:03:41.272
M-A-N-I-S-S-I-P-P-I.

00:03:41.272 --> 00:03:42.414
- That's Mississippi!

00:03:42.414 --> 00:03:43.302
(bell ringing)

00:03:43.302 --> 00:03:44.135
- Wait, what does that mean?

00:03:44.135 --> 00:03:44.968
- [Kate] It's such a close game

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:46.560
and now we're at an extra credit question.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.184
This is for the whole megillah.

00:03:48.184 --> 00:03:49.080
- Here we go.
- Okay, okay.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:49.913
- All right.

00:03:49.913 --> 00:03:52.491
Pennsylvania is known as what?

00:03:52.491 --> 00:03:53.324
(buzzer ringing)
(hands thumping)

00:03:53.324 --> 00:03:54.157
- The Keystone State!

00:03:54.157 --> 00:03:54.990
- You are correct!

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:55.823
(Quinta screaming and clapping)

00:03:55.823 --> 00:03:56.656
(bell tinging)

00:03:56.656 --> 00:03:57.942
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:03:57.942 --> 00:03:59.110
(air horn honking)

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:01.822
(women talking excitedly)

00:04:01.822 --> 00:04:04.407
- I finally won a show!
- She finally won a show!

00:04:04.407 --> 00:04:06.446
- Now you want to work!

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:07.279
(audience laughing)

00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:09.030
- No, here is the difference though,

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:10.980
'cause I saw it in my
peripheral vision. (laughing)

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.960
Yours was like, yours was so grand.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.400
It was like woo!

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.108
And hers was like boop.

00:04:16.108 --> 00:04:16.941
(buzzer ringing)

00:04:16.941 --> 00:04:17.774
And yours was so grand,

00:04:17.774 --> 00:04:18.607
it took a little longer.
- I had to.

00:04:18.607 --> 00:04:19.590
- Can I just tell you,

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:20.970
'cause I was there that night,

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:24.009
this is way more excited than
she was when she won the Emmy.

00:04:24.009 --> 00:04:26.156
(all laughing)

00:04:26.156 --> 00:04:28.650
- She was so stealth.
(hands banging on table)

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.907
- Quinta and Lisa go to
the head of the class!

00:04:30.907 --> 00:04:32.276
Please clap!

00:04:32.276 --> 00:04:33.239
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:34.988
You did it! You did it! You did it!

00:04:34.988 --> 00:04:35.821
Yay!

00:04:35.821 --> 00:04:36.705
- Yay!

00:04:36.705 --> 00:04:37.617
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:04:37.617 --> 00:04:39.510
- We're so happy for y'all.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:40.343
- Sorry guys.

00:04:40.343 --> 00:04:41.760
- Um, sort of, kind of.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:45.180
And since Quinta and Lisa are
smarter than fifth graders,

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.276
and obviously Sheryl and myself,

00:04:47.276 --> 00:04:49.080
their photos will go up

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.958
on "The Chicks Wall of Champs
who beat Kelly Clarkson."

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:52.791
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:04:52.791 --> 00:04:54.009
Congratulations.

00:04:54.009 --> 00:04:54.842
(audience clapping)

00:04:54.842 --> 00:04:57.516
A big thanks to Kate Flannery
for hosting, everybody!

00:04:57.516 --> 00:04:59.217
(everyone clapping and cheering)

00:04:59.217 --> 00:05:00.050
- [Sheryl] A legend.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:03.480
- You can see Kate and
Jane Lynch perform songs

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:04.837
off their hit holiday album,

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:06.930
"A Swingin' Little
Christmas" this December.

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:08.610
Check online for tour dates

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:10.770
and of course, watch Abbott Elementary.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:11.673
Wednesdays on ABC.

